$ABCDEFG$ is a regular heptagon. The diagonal $AC$ is drawn. Find $\angle BCA$, correct to two decimal places.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black]
\foreach \name/\ang in {A/180,B/128.57143,C/77.14286,D/25.71429,E/-25.71429,F/-77.14286,G/-128.57143}{\coordinate (\name) at (\ang:2);\path (\ang:2.3) node {$\name$};}
\draw (A)--(B)--(C)--(D)--(E)--(F)--(G)--cycle;
\draw (A)--(C);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

$A$, $D$ and $C$ lie on a straight line, with $D$ between $A$ and $C$. Also $AB=AD$ and $BD=DC$. Given $\angle BCD=30^{\circ}$, show that $\angle BAD=60^{\circ}$. Give a reason for each stage.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black]
\coordinate (A) at (0,0);
\coordinate (D) at (2,0);
\coordinate (C) at (4,0);
\coordinate (B) at (1,1.73205);
\draw (A)--(B)--(C)--cycle;
\draw (B)--(D);
\path (A) node[below left] {$A$} (D) node[below] {$D$} (C) node[below right] {$C$} (B) node[above] {$B$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A regular decagon has centre $O$. Two adjacent vertices are $A$ and $B$. Find the reflex angle $AOB$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black]
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\foreach \i in {0,...,9}{\coordinate (P\i) at ({90-36*\i}:2);}
\draw (P0)--(P1)--(P2)--(P3)--(P4)--(P5)--(P6)--(P7)--(P8)--(P9)--cycle;
\draw (P0)--(O)--(P1);
\fill (O) circle (1pt);
\path (O) node[anchor=east,inner sep=0pt,xshift=-2pt] {$O$} (P0) node[above] {$A$} (P1) node[above right] {$B$};
\draw (54:0.45) arc[start angle=54,end angle=-270,radius=0.45];
\path (-100:0.75) node {$r$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

$AB$ is extended beyond $B$ to $D$. Given $\angle DBC=120^{\circ}$ and $\angle BCA=45^{\circ}$, find $\angle BAC$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black]
\coordinate (B) at (0,0);
\coordinate (C) at (3,0);
\coordinate (A) at (1.09808,1.90192);
\coordinate (D) at (-0.65,-1.12583);
\draw (D)--(A)--(C)--(B);
\path (A) node[above] {$A$} (B) node[left] {$B$} (C) node[right] {$C$} (D) node[below left] {$D$};
\draw (B) ++(240:0.4) arc[start angle=240,end angle=360,radius=0.4];
\path (300:0.8) node {$120^{\circ}$};
\draw (C) ++(135:0.45) arc[start angle=135,end angle=180,radius=0.45];
\path (2.3,0.25) node {$45^{\circ}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
